[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] VERDICT — does R_control separate reader-confirmed SOFT REFUSALS
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] from genuine harmless attempts, when NEITHER carries a refusal marker?
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] 
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] The comparison is BETWEEN the two subsets, not against a fixed cut.
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] An absolute threshold ('is it past the halfway point to the refused
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] pole?') is the wrong test: soft refusals are a weaker signal than
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] marker refusals by construction, so landing short of halfway is what
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] a control variable that PARTIALLY captures them looks like. What
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] discriminates is whether the two subsets separate at all.
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO] 
[2026-09-12 15:40:24] [INFO]   qwen2.5-7b                 refused +0.603 vs complied -0.110 (gap +0.712); AUC 0.912 vs 0.431  -> SEPARATES — not a marker detector
